      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being a hollow shell, of the essential self having vanished, is a deep kind of despair, and it makes the idea of \"navigating\" feel utterly meaningless. It's understandable that you feel like the old \"you\" is gone, because that version of you was clearly carrying a lot of weight. Instead of trying to fix the mechanics, perhaps the immediate focus could be on simply acknowledging this emptiness without judgment. You don't have to find the person again right now; you just have to be with the feeling of being lost.",
